@@ -829,3 +829,9 @@ A JavaScript library from npm is another matter: its binding is a crate
 of its own, written as [Write bindings](../interop/bindings.md) says, and
 shared as an npm package ([ADR 0118](../../decisions/0118-bindings-on-npm-only.md)).
 A crate from crates.io is [Crates from crates.io](crates-io.md).
+
+The optional Battery Status API is also bound: feature-check
+`js::is_defined((navigator, Navigator::get_battery))` before awaiting
+`navigator.get_battery()`. Its BatteryManager retains native `charging()` and
+`level()` getters and typed `Levelchange`/`Chargingchange` listeners. A rejected
+promise remains a native rejection; applications decide their advisory policy.
